                        "sense_id": "0a158085-5363-3f46-b0ad-3f3eb419eca6",
                        "entry_id": "b64dbb6d-422a-3654-9580-184356781828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The sound made by a horse: an act or instance of the verb neigh."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b89bc507-7772-4e93-a515-e5a2170f637f",
                                "sense_id": "0a158085-5363-3f46-b0ad-3f3eb419eca6",
                                "text": "And when the earth beneath his tameless tread,\nShook with the sullen thunder, he would spread\nHis nostrils to the blast, and joyously\nMock the fierce peal with neighings; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60434d41-7a11-4e9f-8db2-e0be5f2c52a8",
                                "sense_id": "0a158085-5363-3f46-b0ad-3f3eb419eca6",
                                "text": "During the night a neighing of horses was heard, and when day broke, they found these three animals had joined those belonging to our party."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d44db07-a06c-42a7-92fe-8f7aae8155ae",
                                "sense_id": "0a158085-5363-3f46-b0ad-3f3eb419eca6",
                                "text": "Old pigtailed seamen would tell of horseshoes found in the meat casks; of curious barkings and neighings heard in the slaughter-houses; and of negroes who disappeared near the victualling yards, to be seen no more."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
